**File**: `src/state.rs`

**The fix**: Added a diagnostic guard in the `record()` function (the central funnel for all state events). When a `ModelCallCompleted` event is being recorded and `CURRENT_MODEL_CALL_ID` is `None` (meaning no `ModelCallStarted` preceded it), the guard now emits a `ModelCallCompletedWithoutStart` diagnostic event via `recorder.append()` directly.

**Why this works**: The `record()` function is the single entry point for all state events — whether from `prompt.rs`, yoagent's state adapter, or any other codepath. By placing the guard here, every unmatched completion is caught regardless of which codepath produced it. The diagnostic event is recorded using `recorder.append()` directly (not `record()`) to avoid re-entering `ensure_run_started()` or the guard itself.

**What was already present** (from prior work) and is now wired up:
• `EventType::ModelCallCompletedWithoutStart` enum variant (was dead code)
• `event_type_label()` entry for the variant
• `parse_event_type_label()` entry for the variant

